        'Scripture makes the poor a cause to plead, never fundraising copy (Proverbs 31:9; Isaiah 1:17). For a people and a church, what is the difference — in practice, this month — between pleading FOR the vulnerable and raising money OFF them?',
        '"Put not your trust in princes" (Psalm 146:3) and "Ye cannot serve God and mammon" (Matthew 6:24). Where have you — or a community you love — handed a leader, party, or platform a loyalty that belongs only to the King? What would it look like to test their fruit instead (Matthew 7:20)?',
        'Jeremiah 5:31 says a managed narrative works because "my people love to have it so." Where do you prefer a comfortable story over the plumb line — and what would "Prove all things" (1 Thessalonians 5:21) and "Buy the truth, and sell it not" (Proverbs 23:23) cost you this week?',
