          explain: '"He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty" (Psalm 91:1); "pray to thy Father which is in secret" (Matthew 6:6). It is intimacy, not technique. And it does not end in dread: "Resist the devil, and he will flee from you" (James 4:7) — to the living God we watch and pray (Matthew 16:16).',
